      "title": "Dual Career Resources",
      "description": "Dual Career Resources Skip to Content About W&L Academics Admissions & Aid Campus Life Outcomes Alumni Current Students Faculty & Staff Families Visitors | News Events Arts Athletics Giving Dual Career Resources Washington and Lee University Human Resources Work/Life Initiatives Dual Career Resources Human Resources Human Resources Staff Benefits About Our Benefits Program Health, Dental, and Voluntary Vision Benefits Life Insurance Disability Benefits Retirement Savings Plan Computer Purchase Program Educational Grant Program Home Loan Policy Employee Perks Time Off Compensation Staff Compensation Program Emergency Resources for Employees Employee Handbooks and Code of Policies Employee Recognition Employee Resource Group Program Employment Employment Opportunities Information for W&L Employees Information for Supervisors Volunteers and High School Mentoring Program Extended Leaves Short-Term Disability Long-Term Disability Employee Disability Accommodation Policy Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Parental Leave Workplace Injuries, Incidents and Workers' Compensation Learning and Development Staff Continuing Education Program Tuition-Free Courses at Washington and Lee Office Professionals Network (OPN) Training and Development Opportunities AdminConnect PATH The Purpose of PATH Expectations of Employees and Managers PATH Elements PATH Annual Cycle Performance Rating Definitions Employee Development Stages Preparing to Retire Programs and Events Recruitment and Hiring Staff Recruitment Resources Faculty Recruitment Resources Retirees Benefits for Retirees Health Reimbursement Arrangement (HRA) Retiree Health Plan (RHP) Benefits for Survivors of Retirees Resources at Your Fingertips Wellness Live Well W&L 5K Fun Run/Walk Employee Wellness Fair Getting Started with Live Well W&L Incentive Rewards Chart Live Well W&L FAQ Salad Bar Discount Employee Fitness Resources Ergonomic Work Station Assessment Weight Watchers Tobacco/Vaping Cessation Work-Life Initiatives Dependent Care Dual Career Resources W&L Job Openings Local Opportunities Relocating to Lexington Flexible Work Schedules W&L Employee Resource Group (ERG) Program Wellness Program The decision to accept a new position and relocate brings with it the challenge of becoming established in a new geographic area and possibly finding a position for a spouse or partner. Washington and Lee University understands the nature of difficulties that dual career couples face. The Office of Human Resources provides resources to support dual career spouses and partners, and information that is intended to make the transition to the Washington and Lee University community as smooth as possible. The Office of Human Resources provides individualized support to dual career spouses and partners whose employee spouse or partner is in their first year of full-time employment at W&L. This service is extended beyond one year as time allows. Individuals who are interested in dual career services should submit a resume or vitae to the Director of Talent Acquisition. Applicants are also encouraged to initiate conversations with department chairs or supervisors during the interview process. Recruitment Ambassadors In addition to the one-on-one support provided by the Office of Human Resources there are individuals in the W&L community who have agreed to serve as points of contact for new hires and their spouses and partners. Please contact the Director of Talent Acquisition if you wish to reach out to one or more Recruitment Ambassadors to learn more about life at W&L. Dual Career Support Services While we cannot guarantee placement, the Director of Talent Acquisition is available to guide spouses and/ partners as they navigate the job search process. Support includes: Information on the local job market Community information Job search assistance Information on area colleges and universities Networking assistance Relocation information Resume and cover letter review Interview tips Mid-Atlantic Higher Education Recruitment Consortium W&L is a founding member of the Mid-Atlantic Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) , which includes job postings from a variety of colleges, universities and research institutions in the mid-Atlantic region. HERC offers a variety of tools and resources for a successful job search including webinars, articles, and the option to upload a searchable portfolio for potential employers. W&L Job Openings Explore faculty, staff and administrative openings at W&L. Occasionally, departments on campus hire temporary leave replacement from a hiring pool maintained by the Department of Human Resources. Dual career spouses may contact the Director of Talent Acquisition to be added to this list of possible candidates. Local Opportunities Community resources, area colleges and universities, and online job searching. Relocating to Lexington Lexington real estate resources, relocation services, University housing rentals and the W&L home loan program. Human Resources Human Resources Staff Benefits CTO, SLR, Holidays, and Other Time Off Compensation Emergency Resources for Employees Employee Handbooks and Code of Policies Employee Recognition Employee Resource Group Program Employment Extended Leaves Learning and Development PATH Preparing to Retire Programs and Events Recruitment and Hiring Retirees Wellness Work/Life Initiatives Dependent Care Dual Career Resources W&L Job Openings Local Opportunities Relocating to Lexington Flexible Work Schedules W&L Employee Resource Group (ERG) Program Wellness Program W&L Newcomers Club Mid-Atlantic HERC Member Institution Anne Remington Director of Talent Acquisition P: 540-458-8355 E: aremington@wlu.edu Human Resources P: 540-458-8920 F: 540-458-8060 E: humanresources@wlu.edu Mailing Address: Human Resources 204 W. Washington Street Washington and Lee University Lexington, Virginia 24450 Physical Address: 2 S Main Street Lexington, VA 24450 204 W. Washington St. | Lexington VA